  "functions": [
    "FUNC.OP_NEGATE"
  ],
  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "Unary negation coerces text and logicals to numbers and flushes parsed subnormals to +0",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20527.20088, unary negation (-x) coerces its scalar operand to a number (so -\"2\" = -2 and -TRUE = -1, unlike unary +x which leaves text and logicals uncoerced), flushes parsed subnormal literals to +0 (-1E-309 = 0x0000000000000000, not -0.0), and retains a computed subnormal's negated sign when fed a live subnormal value.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured across Excel 16.0.20527.20088 in jnt_operators (rows 5, 6, and 19) and dc_e00t (row 4).",
  "inferred": null,
  "documentation": null,
